{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787598914,"nonce":"yDZbtGn/wZL8Z8hHtKfQG9OjLuY=","message":"Reframe against ADR-0067 (feat/adr-0067-pack-is-the-record) — the CORE of this\nticket is untouched and still the prerequisite for Depot replicas:\n- WorkspaceClient is still a bare reqwest::Client::new()\n  (crates/scarab-workspace-client/src/lib.rs:227) — no connect/request timeout.\n- The fetcher init container is still restart_policy: Never; connection-class\n  and 404 failures still both land in Infra{never_started};\n  NEVER_STARTED_AUTO_ATTEMPTS is still 3; a 20-30s Depot outage during Init\n  still dead-letters the run. All four checklist items stand.\n\nWhat ADR-0067 changed under it (drop these parts of the body when re-reading):\n- It cites 6cb4a27 (Depot HA), now CLOSED — the sequencing decision (\"this\n  lands before HA\") survives; the HA work itself is re-scoped by ADR-0066/0067\n  (fence affinity + packs), not by that ticket.\n- The \"related correction\" that /have is warm-only is FIXED: /have now answers\n  from the durable pack index in Postgres (durable_present_of), so a fresh\n  replica no longer forces a full re-upload. Strike that paragraph.\n- The ledger-rebuildability analysis is obsolete: the write ledger and drain\n  records are Postgres rows (depot_fence_writes / drain records, ADR-0067\n  part 2), replica-independent by construction. The \"ledger but no warm\"\n  asymmetry it worried about is now the DESIGNED state — validate_drain_closure\n  falls back to the durable pack index for warm-missing blobs.\n- The drain half changed shape: one-pass durable into pack sessions. A drain\n  retry after a Depot restart now interacts with in-memory PackSessions (see\n  afb13c2) — the retry story for the DRAIN leg should be designed against\n  sessions, not against the deleted flush.\n- classify_drain still returns FatalConfig for the record-lost case\n  (executor-k8s/src/lib.rs:1775-1797) — that correction is still open.","files":null}]}